## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.10+
- A free [Groq API key](https://console.groq.com/)

### Setup

```bash
# 1. Clone the repo
git clone https://github.com/gaganasindhu-ml/lease-rag-assistant.git
cd lease-rag-assistant

# 2. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 3. Set your Groq API key
export GROQ_API_KEY="your-key-here"        # macOS / Linux
# setx GROQ_API_KEY "your-key-here"        # Windows
```

### Run

```bash
# Ask questions from the command line
python lease_qa_system.py

# Run the evaluation against the golden set
python evaluate.py

# Launch the web app
streamlit run streamlit_app.py
```

---

## Key Design Decisions

**Why split by heading style instead of text patterns?**
The document already tags headings as `Heading 1`. Reading the style is more robust than guessing from text like `startswith("Clause")`, and it keeps working if the wording changes.

**Why attach the clause name to every chunk?**
So every answer can cite its source. A chunk without metadata is just text; it can't tell you where it came from.

**Why instruct the LLM to answer only from the retrieved context?**
To prevent hallucination. When the answer isn't in the retrieved chunks, the system should say so rather than make something up. This is verified with 3 out-of-scope questions.

**Why a hand-written golden set instead of an auto-generated one?**
Generating questions from the same chunks the system retrieves creates *circular evaluation*: the test is built from the answer. A hand-written set is an independent test.

**Why validate that the file is a real `.docx` before parsing?**
A `.docx` is a zip archive. Checking `zipfile.is_zipfile()` first turns a cryptic crash into a clear error message when a file is corrupted, empty, or a Git LFS pointer.

---

## Limitations

- **Single document only**, with no cross-document reasoning
- **Dense retrieval only**, with no hybrid search or re-ranking yet
- **Small corpus** (18 sections); accuracy will differ at scale
- **No confidence scoring** or escalation layer
- **English only**
- **Not legal advice.** Answers reflect the text of one lease; consult a qualified professional for legal decisions

